WEBVTT

00:00.600 --> 00:14.840
You write a script in plain Markdown. Qontent Tube voices every line, animates every scene, and renders a finished video. No timeline dragging, no keyframes, no editing suite.

00:14.840 --> 00:18.120
And everything you just watched was made that way, including me.

00:20.220 --> 00:32.380
Start from a topic. The new tool drafts the script with animation directions and a storyboard for every scene. You review each wireframe, approve it, or lock what you love and regenerate the rest.

00:32.380 --> 00:37.900
No API key? Copy the prompt into any chat, paste the reply, and you get the same checks.

00:40.000 --> 00:49.600
Themes give the stage your colors and fonts in light and dark scenes. Readability is checked as you edit, and one click fixes contrast.

00:51.700 --> 01:02.020
Build a character in seconds. Describe it, pick a style and a personality, lock your favorites. Every character ships rigged, and its mouth follows the real voice, closing in the pauses.

01:04.120 --> 01:13.640
Give a scene its own background, painted from the story and your theme, with a soft veil that keeps every word readable.

01:15.740 --> 01:23.020
Translate to Spanish, French, or any language. Structure stays in sync, voices switch per language, and the storyboard is shared.

01:23.020 --> 01:29.020
Then adapt each scene for Shorts, Reels, and TikTok. The layout reflows. The voice stays.

01:31.120 --> 01:41.680
Render a crisp ten eighty p video with captions and chapters, right on your computer. Qontent Tube zero point two is alive. Go make something people love.
